`ErrorBoundary.tsx` written. Usage:

```tsx
// Default fallback UI
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback
<ErrorBoundary fallback={(err, retry) => (
  <div>
    <p>{err.message}</p>
    <button onClick={retry}>Try again</button>
  </div>
)}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

Key details:
- `getDerivedStateFromError` captures the error into state, triggering the fallback render
- `componentDidCatch` logs `error.message`, `stack`, and React's `componentStack` to `console.error`
- `reset` clears the error state; calling it re-mounts children fresh
- Accepts optional `fallback` prop for custom UI; defaults to a minimal inline fallback with a Retry button
